#!RuleTest
#test FDA-SE1158 expect=violation domain=MB
#note "The FINDINGS arm of the class scope, and the column-absent case: MB flags restraint on row 1 but the dataset carries no MBRSTMOD column at all, so the bare empty(--RSTMOD) leaf is TRUE on every row (absent = all-missing, EC-43) and the rule fires. Plan B phase 4d' deleted the not var_exists(--RSTMOD) disjunct that used to make this a separate branch; the verdict is unchanged. Row 2 indicates no restraint."
#library standard=sendig version=ar-1-0
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=1 nameOnly=MBRSTIND
dataset MB class=FINDINGS label="Microbiology Specimen"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col MBSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col MBTESTCD type=Char label="Microbiology Test or Finding Short Name"
col MBRSTIND type=Char label="Restraint Indicator"
---
S1 | 001 | 1 | AEROBIC | Y
S1 | 001 | 2 | AEROBIC | N
